.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_ACTIVATOR_ACTIVATE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_activator_activate ,
.Nm dtfl_activator_activate_after ,
.Nm dtfl_activator_free ,
.Nm dtfl_sync_activator_activate ,
.Nm dtfl_sync_activator_free
.Nd schedule a timely dataflow operator
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely.h
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_activator_activate "dtfl_activator *a"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_activator_activate_after "dtfl_activator *a" "uint64_t delay_ns"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_activator_free "dtfl_activator *a"
.Ft int
.Fn dtfl_sync_activator_activate "dtfl_sync_activator *a"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_sync_activator_free "dtfl_sync_activator *a"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
An activator marks an operator to be scheduled again, so an operator
that parks waiting on an external event can ask to run once the event
arrives.
Both kinds are obtained from the operator handle with
.Xr dtfl_op_input_next 3 Ap s
.Fn dtfl_op_activator
and
.Fn dtfl_op_sync_activator ,
and the caller frees them.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_activator_activate
marks the operator active for the next step.
.Fn dtfl_activator_activate_after
does so after
.Fa delay_ns
nanoseconds when the worker has a timer, or at once otherwise.
A
.Vt dtfl_activator
belongs to the worker thread.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_sync_activator_activate
marks the operator active from any thread and wakes the worker.
It is the one activation path that may cross threads.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_activator_free
and
.Fn dtfl_sync_activator_free
release the handles.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_sync_activator_activate
returns 0 on success, or
.Dv DTFL_ESTATE
once the worker is gone.
The other functions return no value.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
/* Inside logic: ask to be scheduled again next step. */
dtfl_activator *a = dtfl_op_activator(op);
dtfl_activator_activate(a);
dtfl_activator_free(a);

/* From another thread feeding an external source: */
if (dtfl_sync_activator_activate(sync) == DTFL_ESTATE)
	/* the worker has shut down */ ;
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width DTFL_ESTATE
.It Bq Er DTFL_ESTATE
.Fn dtfl_sync_activator_activate
was called after the worker shut down.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_op_input_next 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_worker_dataflow 3
.Sh HISTORY
These are the C forms of timely's
.Vt Activator
and
.Vt SyncActivator
.Pq activate.rs .
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
A
.Vt dtfl_activator
belongs to its worker thread and must not be shared.
A
.Vt dtfl_sync_activator
is thread-safe: any thread may call
.Fn dtfl_sync_activator_activate .
.Fn dtfl_sync_activator_free
is called from the thread that holds the handle.
